{"chunk_id": "51d5ac169645", "text": "Arjuna, enraged by the death of his son Abhimanyu, swears a terrible oath: if he does not kill Jayadratha in the next day's battle, he will accept the fate of the worst sinners and even enter blazing fire. He invokes a long catalogue of moral transgressions, declaring he will share their cursed destinies if he fails. After this vow, he stretches the Gandiva bow and Krishna sounds the conch Panchajanya, shaking the universe and filling the Pandava camp with triumphant roars. Hearing the uproar and learning of the vow, Jayadratha is overcome with terror and considers fleeing the Kuru camp. Duryodhana, however, reassures him that the greatest Kaurava warriors\u2014Drona, Karna, Kripa, and many others\u2014will surround and protect him. The scene heightens tension for the coming battle, framing Arjuna\u2019s vow as both cosmic and inevitable.\nArjuna vows to kill Jayadratha by sunset or self-immolate, terrifying the Kaurava camp as Jayadratha begs protection from Duryodhana and allied warriors.\nThemes: vengeful oath, honor and vows, fear of heroic power, war strategy, cosmic witnesses", "vector": [0.0051101380959153175, -0.01990264281630516, -0.006068288814276457, 0.01812754198908806, -0.019687479361891747, 0.025550689548254013, -0.01978161372244358, -0.003967080730944872, -0.012943441979587078, -0.008135877549648285, 0.02585998736321926, 0.01058336440473795, 0.01621796377003193, 0.004679810721427202, 0.0024323584511876106, 0.01198192872107029, 0.0512627512216568, -0.00780640821903944, 0.03297383710741997, -0.024945542216300964, -0.010321133770048618, 0.0020575029775500298, 0.002339905360713601, 0.03068772330880165, 0.0007463491056114435, 0.03445308655500412, -0.016460023820400238, -0.019808508455753326, 0.020696058869361877, -0.0043805986642837524, 0.002708036918193102, 0.004639467224478722, 0.0009211695869453251, 0.0013472945429384708, -0.030902886763215065, 0.023103203624486923, -0.009884082712233067, -0.017387917265295982, 0.01